# Photos & RGPD — Clean Connect

> Activé sur `apps/api/src/modules/photos/**`.
> Cahier des charges : §6.4 (sécurité) et §6.5 (RGPD).
> ADRs : [ADR-009 Cloudinary signed upload + dual variant](../../docs/adr/ADR-009-cloudinary-signed-upload-dual-variant.md), [ADR-010 rétention 30 jours](../../docs/adr/ADR-010-photos-retention-30-days.md).

---

## Upload — Signed URL Cloudinary + PhotoUploadSession (ADR-009)

**Principes** :
- Le mobile upload **directement** à Cloudinary (multipart). Le backend ne transite **jamais** le binaire.
- **Interdiction des base64 uploads** (D16 + ADR-009). Multipart direct uniquement.
- **2 variants Cloudinary** par capture : `ORIGINAL` (audit/litige, ADMIN only) + `DISPLAY` (compressé `f_auto,q_auto,w_1600`, EXIF strip, exposé aux acteurs métier). Même `captureClientUuid` pour les deux variants.
- **Idempotence** par `captureClientUuid` (UUID v4 client-generated) + `PhotoUploadSession` (jeton court TTL 5 min).

### Étape 1 — Le mobile demande un presign + ouvre une session

```typescript
// POST /v1/missions/:id/photos/presign
@Post(':id/photos/presign')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles('PRESTATAIRE')
async presign(
  @Param('id', new ZodValidationPipe(uuidSchema)) missionId: string,
  @Body() dto: PresignPhotoUploadInput,
  @CurrentUser() user: AuthUser,
) {
  // dto : { captureClientUuid, variant, phase, mimeType, bytes }
  // 1) Ownership prestataire ACCEPTED sur la mission
  await this.assertCanUploadPhoto(missionId, user)
  // 2) MIME whitelist (image/jpeg|png|heic|webp) + bytes <= 10 MiB (Zod + check Cloudinary preset)
  // 3) Crée PhotoUploadSession (TTL 5 min, token_digest = sha256(opaqueToken))
  const session = await this.sessions.create({
    missionId,
    uploaderUserId: user.id,
    phase: dto.phase,
    captureClientUuid: dto.captureClientUuid,
    maxBytes: 10 * 1024 * 1024,
  })

  // 4) Signature Cloudinary (folder privé)
  const folder = `${env.NODE_ENV}/missions/${missionId}/${dto.phase.toLowerCase()}/${dto.captureClientUuid}`
  const publicId = `${folder}/${dto.variant.toLowerCase()}` // /original ou /display
  const timestamp = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)
  const signature = cloudinary.utils.api_sign_request(
    { public_id: publicId, timestamp, folder, type: 'private' },
    env.CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET,
  )

  return {
    sessionId: session.id,
    sessionToken: session.opaqueToken, // jamais re-loggé
    expiresAt: session.expiresAt.toISOString(),
    cloudinaryParams: { signature, timestamp, publicId, apiKey: env.CLOUDINARY_API_KEY, cloudName: env.CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME, folder, type: 'private' },
  }
}
```

### Étape 2 — Le mobile upload à Cloudinary (multipart direct, EXIF strip + compress mobile-side)

(Côté mobile, voir `mobile.mdc` + skill `offline-sync-pattern`. Le serveur n'intervient pas dans le transit. Le mobile a déjà strippé l'EXIF + compressé via `expo-image-manipulator` AVANT l'upload.)

### Étape 3 — Le mobile confirme l'upload

```typescript
// POST /v1/missions/:id/photos/confirm
@Post(':id/photos/confirm')
@UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
@Roles('PRESTATAIRE')
async confirm(
  @Param('id', new ZodValidationPipe(uuidSchema)) missionId: string,
  @Body() dto: ConfirmPhotoUploadInput,
  @CurrentUser() user: AuthUser,
) {
  const session = await this.sessions.consume(dto.sessionId, dto.sessionToken)
  if (!session) throw new ConflictException({ error: 'PHOTO_UPLOAD_SESSION_ALREADY_CONSUMED' })
  if (session.expiresAt < new Date()) throw new GoneException({ error: 'UPLOAD_SESSION_EXPIRED' }) // HTTP 410

  // Anti cross-session / cross-mission
  if (session.captureClientUuid !== dto.captureClientUuid) {
    throw new ConflictException({ error: 'PHOTO_CAPTURE_CLIENT_UUID_SESSION_MISMATCH' })
  }
  if (session.missionId !== missionId) {
    throw new ConflictException({ error: 'PHOTO_UPLOAD_SESSION_MISSION_MISMATCH' })
  }

  // Crée la ligne Photo (idempotent via UNIQUE(missionId, captureClientUuid, variant))
  return this.photos.upsert({
    missionId,
    captureClientUuid: dto.captureClientUuid,
    variant: dto.variant, // ORIGINAL | DISPLAY
    phase: session.phase,
    cloudinaryPublicId: dto.cloudinaryPublicId,
    checksumSha256: dto.checksumSha256,
    gpsLatitude: dto.gpsLatitude ?? null, // **séparé EXIF** — envoyé explicitement par mobile
    gpsLongitude: dto.gpsLongitude ?? null,
    gpsAccuracyMeters: dto.gpsAccuracyMeters ?? null,
    gpsMissing: !dto.gpsLatitude || !dto.gpsLongitude,
  })
}
```

### Étape 4 — Cloudinary notifie (webhook signé)

```typescript
@Post('cloudinary/webhook')
@HttpCode(HttpStatus.OK)
async cloudinaryWebhook(@Req() req: RawBodyRequest<Request>, @Headers('x-cld-signature') sig: string) {
  // 1. Signature AVANT toute désérialisation
  if (!verifyCloudinarySignature(req.rawBody, sig, env.CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET)) {
    throw new BadRequestException('Invalid signature')
  }
  const body = JSON.parse(req.rawBody.toString())
  if (body.notification_type === 'upload') {
    await this.prisma.photo.update({
      where: { cloudinaryPublicId: body.public_id },
      data: { syncedAt: new Date(), imageWidth: body.width, imageHeight: body.height, bytes: body.bytes },
    })
  }
}
```

