## Idempotence — `captureClientUuid` + `PhotoUploadSession`

**Règle dure** : le mobile génère un UUID v4 **avant** la capture (`captureClientUuid`). Le backend stocke avec contrainte `@@unique([missionId, captureClientUuid, variant])`.

```prisma
model Photo {
  id                   String              @id @db.Uuid // UUID v4 généré côté CLIENT (offline-first)
  missionId            String              @db.Uuid
  mission              Mission             @relation(...)
  type                 PhotoType           // BEFORE | AFTER
  variant              PhotoVariant        @default(DISPLAY) // ORIGINAL | DISPLAY
  captureClientUuid    String              @db.Uuid // OBLIGATOIRE, relie ORIGINAL/DISPLAY
  photoUploadSessionId String?             @db.Uuid
  cloudinaryPublicId   String?             @db.VarChar(1024)
  checksumSha256       String?             @db.VarChar(64)
  gpsLatitude          Decimal?            @db.Decimal(10, 8)
  gpsLongitude         Decimal?            @db.Decimal(11, 8)
  gpsAccuracyMeters    Int?
  gpsMissing           Boolean             @default(false)
  flagSuspicious       Boolean             @default(false)
  syncedAt             DateTime?
  deletedAt            DateTime?           // tombstone post-purge
  createdAt            DateTime            @default(now())

  @@unique([missionId, captureClientUuid, variant])
  @@index([missionId, type])
}

model PhotoUploadSession {
  id                String    @id @default(uuid()) @db.Uuid
  missionId         String    @db.Uuid
  uploaderUserId    String    @db.Uuid
  phase             PhotoType
  tokenDigest       String    @unique @db.VarChar(64) // sha256(opaqueToken) — secret jamais stocké
  expiresAt         DateTime
  consumedAt        DateTime?
  maxBytes          Int       @default(10485760) // 10 MiB
  createdAt         DateTime  @default(now())
}
```

Si le mobile retry par erreur, le serveur renvoie la photo existante (upsert idempotent) sans rien dupliquer. **Session expirée** = `410 UPLOAD_SESSION_EXPIRED` (distinct de 409, sémantique HTTP correcte).

